                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>At his news conference of March 17, 1954, President Eisenhower responded to questions concerning the possibility of
                    the outbreak of general war occurring as the outgrowth of a situation like
                    Indochina, the response of the United States should large-scale aggression take
                    place, and the status of the military situation in Indochina. For the record of
                    the news conference, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents
                        of the United States: Dwight D.
                            Eisenhower, 1954</hi>, pages 320–332.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
